  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investments in Forests and Sustainable Land Use Phase 2 - Component 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Component 3: Business and market development in &#x2018;thin&#x2019; markets (of the Congo Basin)

Component 3 will provide grant funding to land sector interventions in Congo Basin countries that build sustainable production capacity, elementary market infrastructure, mobilise pioneer investment, enhance long-term private sector capacity and support business environment reform. This will encompass supply-side partnerships, demand-side measures and enabling conditions interventions. It will include business-led and smallholder-oriented solutions, with an exclusive focus on Congo Basin countries. Although they vary considerably, the operating contexts of Congo Basin countries typically present particularly difficult challenges for business-led and private-investment oriented sustainability solutions and carry particularly high costs and risks of &#x2018;doing business&#x2019; for both private sector actors and donor-funded interventions. The precise intervention areas and discrete activities that will be supported by this programme component can only be fully determined in delivery, following rigorous analysis of the local context by the programme&#x2019;s delivery partner.</narrative>
  </description>
